            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0279" n="185" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg185"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.01/18: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Higgins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-23T12:00:00-06:00">December 23,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 5:05 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>130. Department’s telegram No. 93, December 20, 8 p.m.<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d144-f1"/> Minister for Foreign Affairs states that his Government’s
                    policy will conform to that of the United States Government with regard to the
                    recognition of the Guatemalan Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Higgins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
